# Normalise line endings.
#
# Every file this repo tracks is text (md, js, html, json, gs). Editing on
# Windows was rewriting whole files as CRLF, so git reported all ~11,000 lines
# of a 20-line change as modified and real edits became unreviewable.
#
# text=auto  — git stores text as LF in the repository, whatever the checkout did.
# eol=lf     — and checks it back out as LF, so the working tree stops drifting.
#
# Binary files are detected automatically by text=auto and are left untouched.
# There are none tracked today; this keeps it that way if one is ever added.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the extensions actually in the tree, so intent is explicit
# rather than inferred.
*.html  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.gs    text eol=lf
